# Configuration for the bbq-predictor publisher, run every five minutes by
# the systemd timer or, where systemd is not running, by cron
# (bbq-predictor-publish(1)).
#
# BBQ_STATION is required: nothing is fetched without it rather than
# fetching for a station nobody named. It is a Weather Underground
# personal weather station id -- the applet's station list shows the
# ones near you, and its "Find..." button searches elsewhere.
#
#BBQ_STATION=ISTOCK877
#
# Every round publishes the station's signed files for bbq-predictor-serve
# (project.md sec 15.12). The key is made once, as the account that
# publishes:
#
#   sudo -u bbq-predictor bbq-predictor-publish \
#           --generate-signing-key /var/lib/bbq-predictor/signing.key
#
# and the public key it prints is what the applet is built with. Until it
# exists, a round with a station set refuses before fetching and says so.
#
# The tree and the key default to these. Under systemd only the state
# directory is writable, so a tree elsewhere needs a ReadWritePaths= drop-in.
#
#BBQ_PUBLISH_DIR=/var/lib/bbq-predictor/published
#BBQ_SIGNING_KEY=/var/lib/bbq-predictor/signing.key
